  "title": "Rest eyes open",
  "description": "Resting-state EEG dataset from 149 participants, including 100 individuals with Parkinson's disease and 49 controls. Recordings were acquired with a 64-channel BrainVision system during two minutes of eyes-open rest. The data support investigation of neural correlates of cognitive dysfunction in Parkinson's disease.",
  "methods_description": "Resting-state EEG was recorded with a 64-channel BrainVision cap while participants sat in a quiet room with their eyes open for two minutes.",
